WEBVTT

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.980
Scratches on polished bedrock give the axis of former ice

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:04.760
flow.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.460
A plucked face can resolve which way along that axis ice

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:10.460
traveled.

00:00:10.835 --> 00:00:14.235
A boulder dropped from floating ice can interrupt much finer

00:00:14.235 --> 00:00:15.455
sediment below.

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:19.980
Evaporation moves proportionally more light oxygen into the

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:20.740
vapor.

00:00:21.065 --> 00:00:24.245
When growing ice sheets store more of that light oxygen on

00:00:24.245 --> 00:00:27.645
land, the remaining ocean grows relatively richer in heavy

00:00:27.645 --> 00:00:28.585
oxygen.

00:00:29.195 --> 00:00:32.355
Higher marine shell ratios mark glacial intervals in this

00:00:32.355 --> 00:00:33.095
graph.

00:00:33.415 --> 00:00:37.555
The Greenland graph instead plots inferred temperature along

00:00:37.555 --> 00:00:39.175
its horizontal axis.
